  "sourceType": "CLASSIC",
  "sourceNotes": "Lekach is documented in Ashkenazi Jewish cookery from at least the 18th century and appears in foundational Jewish cookery references including the Vilna gaon's community cookbooks and later in Joan Nathan's Jewish Cooking in America (1994) and Leah Koenig's Modern Jewish Cooking (2015). The characteristic dark colour and moist crumb come from the use of both honey and black tea; the spice combination varies by family tradition. Adding tea or coffee to the batter is a consistent feature across documented recipes.",
