  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Honey cake is a one-bowl bake: all the wet ingredients go in together, the dry ingredients are sifted in, and the whole thing is stirred to a smooth batter. The strong black tea adds tannin and depth without any discernible tea flavour. Orange zest cuts through the sweetness of the honey and brightens the spice. Do not be alarmed by how liquid the batter seems; it bakes into a moist, dense crumb."
          }
        ]
      },
