          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make the batter"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Heat the oven to 170°C (conventional). Grease and line a 900 g loaf tin with baking paper. Whisk {{honey}}, {{dark-brown-sugar}}, {{vegetable-oil}}, {{eggs}}, the zest of {{orange}}, and the brewed {{water}} (strong black tea) together in a large bowl until smooth. Sift in {{plain-flour}}, {{baking-powder}}, {{bicarbonate-of-soda}}, {{cinnamon-ground}}, {{mixed-spice}}, {{cardamom-ground}}, and {{sea-salt-fine}}. Stir until just combined; a few small lumps are fine. The batter will be quite liquid."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Bake"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pour the batter into the prepared tin. Bake for 55 to 65 minutes until a skewer inserted into the centre comes out clean. Cover loosely with foil after 35 minutes if the top is darkening too quickly; the honey gives the cake a deep brown crust. Leave in the tin for 15 minutes, then turn out onto a wire rack. The cake keeps well and improves over 2 to 3 days wrapped at room temperature."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
